[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TyreClass" load_steps=2 format=3]

; Factors as responses (dry x factor) over the all-season tyre; brackets are docs/sources.md. dry 1.10: an SUV-size test put the best all-season 6.5 m (18 %) behind the summer reference's 37.0 m [70]; car sizes run closer (estimate). Snow 0.61 in all: twice a winter tyre's 50 km/h stop, 62 m against the all-season's 38 [67]; Wong's packed snow 0.20 is this tyre (Surface). Ice 0.74 in all: 35.5 m against 26.2 from 40 km/h [71]. Field, grass and mud factors 0.9: fewer voids (estimate). crr: label B against the all-season's C, 2020/740 [74].

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/vehicles/base/tyre_class.gd" id="1_tyre"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_tyre")
